  "notes": "{命|めい}じる is a formal verb meaning 'to order' or 'to command,' used in official or hierarchical contexts.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- No standard intransitive pair\n- Pattern: [noun]⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{命|めい}じる\n\nALTERNATE FORM:\n- {命|めい}ずる (classical/literary variant)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧〜⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{命|めい}じる: to order someone to do something\n- 〜⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{命|めい}じられる: to be ordered to ~\n\nSIMILAR WORDS (less formal → more formal):\n- ⟦{頼|たの}む→頼む：01104_tanomu⟧: to ask, request\n- ⟦{指示|しじ}する→指示する：26845_shijisuru⟧: to instruct\n- ⟦{命令|めいれい}する→命令する：26833_meireisuru⟧: to order (noun + suru)\n- {命|めい}じる: to command (most formal)\n\nUSAGE:\nPrimarily used in business, military, or official contexts where clear hierarchy exists.",
